      "topic": "Solar System",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Sun The Sun is the Solar System's star and by far its most massive component.Its large mass (332,900 Earth masses), which comprises 99.86% of all the mass in the Solar System, produces temperatures and densities in its core high enough to sustain nuclear fusion of hydrogen into helium.This releases an enormous amount of energy, mostly radiated into space as electromagnetic radiation peaking in visible light.",
