      "orginal_content": "Mars-crossing asteroids are those with perihelia above 1.3 AU which cross the orbit of Mars.As of 2024, NASA lists 26,182 confirmed Mars-crossing asteroids.Asteroid belt The asteroid belt occupies a torus-shaped region between 2.3 and 3.3 AU from the Sun, which lies between the orbits of Mars and Jupiter.It is thought to be remnants from the Solar System's formation that failed to coalesce because of the gravitational interference of Jupiter.",
