      "topic": "Solar System",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Hilda asteroids are in a 3:2 resonance with Jupiter; that is, they go around the Sun three times for every two Jovian orbits.They lie in three linked clusters between Jupiter and the main asteroid belt.Trojans are bodies located within another body's gravitationally stable Lagrange points: L4, 60\u00b0 ahead in its orbit, or L5, 60\u00b0 behind in its orbit.Every planet except Mercury is known to possess at least one trojan.The Jupiter trojan population is roughly equal to that of the asteroid belt.After Jupiter, Neptune possesses the most confirmed trojans, at 28.Outer Solar System The outer region of the Solar System is home to the giant planets and their large moons.The centaurs and many short-period comets orbit in this region.",
