      "orginal_content": "It is composed mainly of small Solar System bodies, although the largest few are probably large enough to be dwarf planets.There are estimated to be over 100,000 Kuiper belt objects with a diameter greater than 50 km (30 mi), but the total mass of the Kuiper belt is thought to be only a tenth or even a hundredth the mass of Earth.Many Kuiper belt objects have satellites, and most have orbits that are substantially inclined (~10\u00b0) to the plane of the ecliptic.The Kuiper belt can be roughly divided into the \"classical\" belt and the resonant trans-Neptunian objects.",
      "headers": [
