      "orginal_content": "Orcus (30.3\u201348.1 AU), is in the same 2:3 orbital resonance with Neptune as Pluto, and is the largest such object after Pluto itself.Its eccentricity and inclination are similar to Pluto's, but its perihelion lies about 120\u00b0 from that of Pluto.Thus, the phase of Orcus's orbit is opposite to Pluto's: Orcus is at aphelion (most recently in 2019) around when Pluto is at perihelion (most recently in 1989) and vice versa.For this reason, it has been called the anti-Pluto.It has one known moon, Vanth.",
