      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Like Pluto, its orbit is highly eccentric, with a perihelion of 38.2 AU (roughly Pluto's distance from the Sun) and an aphelion of 97.6 AU, and steeply inclined to the ecliptic plane at an angle of 44\u00b0.Gonggong (33.8\u2013101.2 AU) is a dwarf planet in a comparable orbit to Eris, except that it is in a 3:10 resonance with Neptune.It has one known moon, Xiangliu.",
