      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Extreme trans-Neptunian objects Some objects in the Solar System have a very large orbit, and therefore are much less affected by the known giant planets than other minor planet populations.These bodies are called extreme trans-Neptunian objects, or ETNOs for short.Generally, ETNOs' semi-major axes are at least 150\u2013250 AU wide.",
