      "orginal_content": "The scientific study of the Sun is called heliology.General characteristics The Sun is a G-type main-sequence star that makes up about 99.86% of the mass of the Solar System.The Sun is classed as a G2 star, meaning it is a G-type star, with 2 indicating its surface temperature is in the second range of the G class.It has an absolute magnitude of +4.83, estimated to be brighter than about 85% of the stars in the Milky Way, most of which are red dwarfs.It is more massive than 95% of the stars within 7 pc (23 ly).The Sun is a Population I, or heavy-element-rich, star.",
