      "topic": "Sun",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Solar space missions The first satellites designed for long-term observation of the Sun from interplanetary space were Pioneer 6, 7, 8, and 9, launched by NASA between 1959 and 1968.These probes orbited the Sun at a distance similar to that of Earth, and made the first detailed measurements of the solar wind and the solar magnetic field.",
