      "topic": "Sun",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "In the 1970s, two Helios spacecraft and the Skylab Apollo Telescope Mount provided scientists with significant new data on solar wind and the solar corona.The Helios 1 and 2 probes were U.S.\u2013German collaborations that studied the solar wind from an orbit carrying the spacecraft inside Mercury's orbit at perihelion.",
