      "topic": "Sun",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "The Skylab space station, launched by NASA in 1973, included a solar observatory module called the Apollo Telescope Mount that was operated by astronauts resident on the station.Skylab made the first time-resolved observations of the solar transition region and of ultraviolet emissions from the solar corona.Discoveries included the first observations of coronal mass ejections, then called \"coronal transients\", and of coronal holes, now known to be intimately associated with the solar wind.",
