      "topic": "Sun",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Elemental abundances in the photosphere are well known from spectroscopic studies, but the composition of the interior of the Sun is more poorly understood.A solar wind sample return mission, Genesis, was designed to allow astronomers to directly measure the composition of solar material.",
