      "id": "8dc4100f-7616-42e7-8303-a9b7e3e84716",
      "topic": "Sun",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Many ancient monuments were constructed with solar phenomena in mind; for example, stone megaliths mark the summer or winter solstice (for example in Nabta Playa, Egypt; Mnajdra, Malta; and Stonehenge, England); Newgrange, a prehistoric human-built mount in Ireland, was designed to detect the winter solstice; the pyramid of El Castillo at Chich\u00e9n Itz\u00e1 in Mexico is designed to cast shadows in the shape of serpents climbing the pyramid at the vernal and autumnal equinoxes.",
      "headers": [
        "Solar Alignment in Ancient Monuments",
        "Solstice and Equinox Alignments",
        "Examples of Solar-Aligned Structures",
        "Ancient Astronomical Observations"
      ]
