      "topic": "Moon",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Additionally the Moon moves ~27% of the time, or 5\u20136 days per lunar month in Earth's magnetotail, replacing solar wind with Earth wind.Atmosphere The Moon has an atmosphere consisting of only an exosphere, which is so tenuous as to be nearly vacuum, with a total mass of less than 10 tonnes (9.8 long tons; 11 short tons).The surface pressure of this small mass is around 3 \u00d7 10\u221215 atm (0.3 nPa); it varies with the lunar day.Its sources include outgassing and sputtering, a product of the bombardment of lunar soil by solar wind ions.Elements that have been detected include sodium and potassium, produced by sputtering (also found in the atmospheres of Mercury and Io); helium-4 and neon from the solar wind; and argon-40, radon-222, and polonium-210, outgassed after their creation by radioactive decay within the crust and mantle.The absence of such neutral species (atoms or molecules) as oxygen, nitrogen, carbon, hydrogen and magnesium, which are present in the regolith, is not understood.",
