      "id": "c853c41b-9045-4cf4-9095-582a7c7866d9",
      "topic": "Moon",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Mare Frigoris, a basin near the north pole long assumed to be geologically dead, has cracked and shifted.Since the Moon does not have tectonic plates, its tectonic activity is slow, and cracks develop as it loses heat.Scientists have confirmed the presence of a cave on the Moon near the Sea of Tranquility, not far from the 1969 Apollo 11 landing site.The cave, identified as an entry point to a collapsed lava tube, is roughly 45 meters wide and up to 80 m long.This discovery marks the first confirmed entry point to a lunar cave.The analysis was based on photos taken in 2010 by NASA's Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter.",
