      "orginal_content": "Presence of water Liquid water cannot persist on the lunar surface.When exposed to solar radiation, water quickly decomposes through a process known as photodissociation and is lost to space.However, since the 1960s, scientists have hypothesized that water ice may be deposited by impacting comets or possibly produced by the reaction of oxygen-rich lunar rocks, and hydrogen from solar wind, leaving traces of water which could possibly persist in cold, permanently shadowed craters at either pole on the Moon.",
