      "orginal_content": "In 2009, LCROSS sent a 2,300 kg (5,100 lb) impactor into a permanently shadowed polar crater, and detected at least 100 kg (220 lb) of water in a plume of ejected material.Another examination of the LCROSS data showed the amount of detected water to be closer to 155 \u00b1 12 kg (342 \u00b1 26 lb).",
