      "topic": "Moon",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "In 2022, South Korea launched Danuri successfully, its first lunar probe, from the US.In 2023 and 2024, India and Japan became the fourth and fifth country to soft land a spacecraft on the Moon, following the Soviet Union and United States in the 1960s, and China in 2013.Notably, Japan's spacecraft, the Smart Lander for Investigating Moon, survived three lunar nights.In February 2024, the IM-1 lander became the first commercially built lander to land on the Moon.China launched Chang'e 6 in May 2024, which conducted the first sample return from the far side of the Moon.It also carried a Chinese rover to conduct infrared spectroscopy of lunar surface.Pakistan sent a lunar orbiter called ICUBE-Q along with Chang'e 6.Nova-C 2, iSpace Lander and Blue Ghost were all launched to the Moon in 2024.NASA's Artemis II crewed lunar flyby mission launched in April 2026.It was the first crewed mission around the Moon since the Apollo era.Christina Koch became the first woman, Victor Glover the first person of color, Canadian Jeremy Hansen the first non-American, and commander Reid Wiseman the oldest person, to leave low Earth orbit and to fly around the Moon.",
