      "orginal_content": "The surface of Mars as seen from Earth is divided into two kinds of areas, with differing albedo.The paler plains covered with dust and sand rich in reddish iron oxides were once thought of as Martian \"continents\" and given names like Arabia Terra (land of Arabia) or Amazonis Planitia (Amazonian plain).The dark features were thought to be seas, hence their names Mare Erythraeum, Mare Sirenum and Aurorae Sinus.The largest dark feature seen from Earth is Syrtis Major Planum.",
