      "orginal_content": "Tectonic sites The large canyon, Valles Marineris (Latin for Mariner Valleys, also known as Agathodaemon in the old canal maps), has a length of 4,000 kilometres (2,500 mi) and a depth of up to 7 kilometres (4.3 mi).The length of Valles Marineris is equivalent to the length of Europe and extends across one-fifth the circumference of Mars.By comparison, the Grand Canyon on Earth is only 446 kilometres (277 mi) long and nearly 2 kilometres (1.2 mi) deep.",
