      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Holes and caves Images from the Thermal Emission Imaging System (THEMIS) aboard NASA's Mars Odyssey orbiter have revealed seven possible cave entrances on the flanks of the volcano Arsia Mons.The caves, named after loved ones of their discoverers, are collectively known as the \"seven sisters\".Cave entrances measure from 100 to 252 metres (328 to 827 ft) wide and they are estimated to be at least 73 to 96 metres (240 to 315 ft) deep.Because light does not reach the floor of most of the caves, they may extend much deeper than these lower estimates and widen below the surface.\"Dena\" is the only exception; its floor is visible and was measured to be 130 metres (430 ft) deep.",
