      "topic": "Mars",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Human observations and exploration The history of observations of Mars is marked by oppositions of Mars when the planet is closest to Earth and hence is most easily visible, which occur every couple of years.Even more notable are the perihelic oppositions of Mars, which are distinguished because Mars is close to perihelion, making it even closer to Earth.Ancient observations The ancient Sumerians named Mars Nergal, the god of war and plague.During Sumerian times, Nergal was a minor deity of little significance, but, during later times, his main cult center was the city of Nineveh.",
