      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "These maps notably contained features he called canali, which, with the possible exception of the natural canyon Valles Marineris, were later shown to be an optical illusion.These canali were supposedly long, straight lines on the surface of Mars, to which he gave names of famous rivers on Earth.His term, which means \"channels\" or \"grooves\", was popularly mistranslated in English as \"canals\".",
