      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Influenced by the observations, the orientalist Percival Lowell founded an observatory which had 30- and 45-centimetre (12- and 18-in) telescopes.The observatory was used for the exploration of Mars during the last good opportunity in 1894, and the following less favorable oppositions.He published several books on Mars and life on the planet, which had a great influence on the public.",
