      "topic": "Mars",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "The seasonal changes (consisting of the diminishing of the polar caps and the dark areas formed during Martian summers) in combination with the canals led to speculation about life on Mars, and it was a long-held belief that Mars contained vast seas and vegetation.As bigger telescopes were used, fewer long, straight canali were observed.During observations in 1909 by Antoniadi with an 84-centimetre (33 in) telescope, irregular patterns were observed, but no canali were seen.",
