      "topic": "Mars",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Impact glass, formed by the impact of meteors, which on Earth can preserve signs of life, has also been found on the surface of the impact craters on Mars.Likewise, the glass in impact craters on Mars could have preserved signs of life, if life existed at the site.The Cheyava Falls rock discovered on Mars in June 2024 has been designated by NASA as a \"potential biosignature\" and was core sampled by the Perseverance rover for possible return to Earth and further examination.Although highly intriguing, no definitive final determination on a biological or abiotic origin of this rock can be made with the data currently available.",
