      "orginal_content": "Since the volume within the Schwarzschild radius increases with the cube of the radius, average density of a black hole inside its Schwarzschild radius is inversely proportional to the square of its mass: supermassive black holes are much less dense than stellar black holes.The average density of a 108 M\u2609 black hole is comparable to that of water.",
