      "topic": "Black Hole",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "These systems actively emit X-rays for only several months once every 10\u201350 years.During the period of low X-ray emission, called quiescence, the accretion disk is extremely faint, allowing detailed observation of the companion star.",
      "headers": [
