      "topic": "Galaxy",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Bars are thought to be temporary structures that can occur as a result of a density wave radiating outward from the core, or else due to a tidal interaction with another galaxy.Many barred spiral galaxies are active, possibly as a result of gas being channeled into the core along the arms.The Milky Way is a large disk-shaped barred-spiral galaxy about 30 kiloparsecs in diameter and a kiloparsec thick.It contains about two hundred billion (2\u00d71011) stars and has a total mass of about six hundred billion (6\u00d71011) times the mass of the Sun.",
