      "topic": "Galaxy",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Magnetic fields Galaxies have magnetic fields of their own.A galaxy's magnetic field influences its dynamics in multiple ways, including affecting the formation of spiral arms and transporting angular momentum in gas clouds.The latter effect is particularly important, as it is a necessary factor for the gravitational collapse of those clouds, and thus for star formation.",
