      "topic": "Galaxy",
      "source": "Space & Astronomy_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Even seemingly confirmed spectroscopic evidence may turn out to have other origins.For example, astronomers reported HeII emission evidence for Population III stars in the Cosmos Redshift 7 galaxy, with a redshift value of 6.60.Subsequent observations found metallic emission lines, OIII, inconsistent with an early-galaxy star.Evolution Once stars begin to form, emit radiation, and in some cases explode, the process of galaxy formation becomes very complex, involving interactions between the forces of gravity, radiation, and thermal energy.",
