      "orginal_content": "Classical electromagnetism presumed a medium, an luminiferous aether to support the propagation of waves, but this medium could not be detected.The intensity of light from hot glowing blackbody objects did not match the predictions of thermodynamics and electromagnetism.The character of electron emission of illuminated metals differed from predictions.",
