    {
      "id": "23bc5e03-7aae-44d6-b1ea-c3b4148af647",
      "topic": "Physics",
      "source": "Science_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Electricity and magnetism have been studied as a single branch of physics since the intimate connection between them was discovered in the early 19th century; an electric current gives rise to a magnetic field, and a changing magnetic field induces an electric current.Electrostatics deals with electric charges at rest, electrodynamics with moving charges, and magnetostatics with magnetic poles at rest.",
