      "topic": "Chemistry",
      "source": "Science_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Modern principles The current model of atomic structure is the quantum mechanical model.Traditional chemistry starts with the study of elementary particles, atoms, molecules, substances, metals, crystals and other aggregates of matter.Matter can be studied in solid, liquid, gas and plasma states, in isolation or in combination.The interactions, reactions and transformations that are studied in chemistry are usually the result of interactions between atoms, leading to rearrangements of the chemical bonds which hold atoms together.Such behaviors are studied in a chemistry laboratory.The chemistry laboratory stereotypically uses various forms of laboratory glassware.However glassware is not central to chemistry, and a great deal of experimental (as well as applied/industrial) chemistry is done without it.",
