      "orginal_content": "Compound A compound is a pure chemical substance composed of more than one element.The properties of a compound bear little similarity to those of its elements.The standard nomenclature of compounds is set by the International Union of Pure and Applied Chemistry (IUPAC).Organic compounds are named according to the organic nomenclature system.The names for inorganic compounds are created according to the inorganic nomenclature system.When a compound has more than one component, then they are divided into two classes, the electropositive and the electronegative components.",
