      "topic": "Genetics",
      "source": "Science_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "Environment plays a major role in effects of the human genetic disease phenylketonuria.The mutation that causes phenylketonuria disrupts the ability of the body to break down the amino acid phenylalanine, causing a toxic build-up of an intermediate molecule that, in turn, causes severe symptoms of progressive intellectual disability and seizures.However, if someone with the phenylketonuria mutation follows a strict diet that avoids this amino acid, they remain normal and healthy.",
