      "id": "11d0874b-b8af-49b4-a144-d6b237ecf429",
      "topic": "Quantum Mechanics",
      "source": "Science_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "In one of them, a mathematical entity called the wave function provides information, in the form of probability amplitudes, about what measurements of a particle's energy, momentum, and other physical properties may yield.Overview and fundamental concepts Quantum mechanics allows the calculation of properties and behaviour of physical systems.It is typically applied to microscopic systems: molecules, atoms and subatomic particles.It has been demonstrated to hold for complex molecules with thousands of atoms, but its application to human beings raises philosophical problems, such as Wigner's friend, and its application to the universe as a whole remains speculative.Predictions of quantum mechanics have been verified experimentally to an extremely high degree of accuracy.For example, the refinement of quantum mechanics for the interaction of light and matter, known as quantum electrodynamics (QED), has been shown to agree with experiment to within 1 part in 1012 when predicting the magnetic properties of an electron.",
