      "topic": "Quantum Mechanics",
      "source": "Science_wikipedia",
      "orginal_content": "For example, a quantum particle like an electron can be described by a wave function, which associates to each point in space a probability amplitude.Applying the Born rule to these amplitudes gives a probability density function for the position that the electron will be found to have when an experiment is performed to measure it.This is the best the theory can do; it cannot say for certain where the electron will be found.",
