      "original_content": "A number of Arab Muslim scholars wrote about evolution, most notably Ibn Khaldun, who wrote the book Muqaddimah in 1377, in which he asserted that humans developed from \"the world of the monkeys\", in a process by which \"species become more numerous\".",
