      "original_content": "This created the orogeny, or process of mountain building, of the Himalayas.The middle and stiffer layer continued to push into Tibet, causing crustal thickening of the Tibetan Plateau.Immediately south of the emerging Himalayas, plate movement created a vast crescent-shaped trough that rapidly filled with river-borne sediment and now constitutes the Indo-Gangetic Plain.The original Indian plate makes its first appearance above the sediment in the ancient Aravalli range, which extends from the Delhi Ridge in a southwesterly direction.To the west lies the Thar Desert, the eastern spread of which is checked by the Aravallis.",
