      "original_content": "The classic American diner, a casual restaurant type originally intended for the working class, emerged during the 19th century from converted railroad dining cars made stationary.The diner soon evolved into purpose-built structures whose number expanded greatly in the 20th century.The American fast-food industry developed alongside the nation's car culture.American restaurants developed the drive-in format in the 1920s, which they began to replace with the drive-through format by the 1940s.",
